## 🔍 Side-by-Side Code Comparison

### 1. Basic Route Handler

#### ❌ ORIGINAL (INSECURE)
```javascript
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  res.json([
    { id: 1, name: 'Alice', email: 'alice@example.com' },
    { id: 2, name: 'Bob', email: 'bob@example.com' },
  ]);
});
```

**Problems:**
- No authentication required
- Exposes user emails to anyone
- No rate limiting
- No input validation
- No authorization checks

#### ✅ SECURE VERSION
```javascript
app.get('/api/users', 
  authenticateAPIKey,           // Authentication
  requireRole(['admin', 'user']), // Authorization
  strictLimiter,                 // Rate limiting
  [
    query('page').optional().isInt({ min: 1 }),
    query('limit').optional().isInt({ min: 1, max: 100 }),
    query('search').optional().trim().escape()
  ],                             // Input validation
  validateRequest,
  (req, res) => {
    try {
      const users = [/* data */];
      const sanitizedUsers = users.map(sanitizeUser); // Remove sensitive fields

      res.json({
        data: sanitizedUsers,
        pagination: { /* pagination info */ }
      });
    } catch (error) {
      logSecurityEvent('ERROR', req, { error: error.message });
      res.status(500).json({ 
        error: 'Internal server error',
        message: sanitizeError(error)
      });
    }
  }
);
```

**Improvements:**
- ✅ Requires valid API key
- ✅ Role-based access control
